-- Test Case Design: Password Field Validation
-- Using Equivalence Partitioning (EP) & Boundary Value Analysis (BVA)

-- 1. Objective

-- Design a complete, defensible set of test cases for the Password field on a login/registration form, 
   using two core black-box test design techniques:

-- Equivalence Partitioning (EP) — divides input data into classes that the system is expected to treat identically, 
   so we test one representative value per class instead of every possible value.

-- Boundary Value Analysis (BVA) — extends EP by targeting the edges of each partition, 
   since defects statistically cluster at boundaries (off-by-one errors, < vs <=, incorrect loop limits, etc.).
